description: WebSocket market data, stale quotes, and high-frequency UI rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Market data (mandatory)

- Live prices, order books, and charts come from a remote data source (WebSocket when required) plus a local cache.
- Always expose connection and freshness: `live` | `stale` | `disconnected`. Show that in UI via Cubit state.
- Never submit a trade, swap, or order on a stale or disconnected quote. The Use Case must reject it.
- Do not block the UI on each tick. Throttle / sample high-frequency updates. Use `BlocSelector` or equivalent to limit rebuilds.
- Offline: show last cached values as stale, not as live.

```text
❌ BAD — Cubit treats last tick as current; widget rebuilds the whole page per tick
✅ GOOD — quote.freshness == live required to submit; only the price widget rebuilds
```
